WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.156 --> 00:00:02.680
(audience applauding)

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:03.853
- Greetings all.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.850
You know what the
toughest part about being

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.400
a gay, black police officer is?

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.800
The discrimination.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.481
(audience laughing)

00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:14.360
- What?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.924
- Drum roll please.

00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:18.507
(slow tapping)

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.223
That's your drum roll?

00:00:21.223 --> 00:00:22.190
- When a tempo isn't specified,

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.230
any reasonable person
would default to lento.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.490
- Well, it's terrible and
you ruined a fun thing.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.680
- He wrote, "The number
eight, equal sign, equal sign,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.460
equal sign, equal sign,
equal sign, equal sign,

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.637
equal sign, capital 'd'.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.910
Oh, I see what this is.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.860
This is a--
- Yep.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.070
- Wow, that's...

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.570
fantastic news.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.640
- She's worried about her
motorcycle sitting idle,

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.850
so she wants us to take
it out once a day, here.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.350
- I think you should do this,
you're more the biker type.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.390
I've seen you use a toothpick in public.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.970
- Motorcycles are death machines,

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:01.080
I have three kids, I'm not risking it.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.060
- Are you saying my life matters less

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.050
because I don't conform

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.550
to societies heteronormative
child-centric ideals?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.660
- Are you really playing
the gay card right now?

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.721
- Yas queen.

00:01:10.721 --> 00:01:12.880
(keys jangling)
(fingers snapping)

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.740
Pay no attention to him, Rosa.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.340
He's very emotional, Rosa.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.200
- Why are you saying my first name?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.400
- Well, Rosa, I read an
article in a medical journal

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.250
that said one destabilizing
aspect of incarceration

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.860
is the constant dehumanization, Rosa.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.890
You need to be reminded

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.030
that you are more than
just a number, Rosa.

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.010
You are Rosa...

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:31.843
Rosa.

00:01:31.843 --> 00:01:32.770
- Yep, that fixes prison.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.460
- I've been on the phone six hours

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.710
and I just want to cancel an account.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.880
Yes, you've mentioned the bundles

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.180
and I don't want home phone service!

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.560
No, do not transfer me Rodrigo.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.680
No, no!

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.513
No Rodrigo!

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:46.770
- Hey there Captain.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.800
Oh, is this your new assistant?

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.030
- John Herbland, nice to meet ya.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:50.770
- And John Herbland has just been fired.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:51.647
- What?
- I have?

00:01:51.647 --> 00:01:54.930
- "Meet ya", you just
abbreviated a one syllable word.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:55.763
- [Jake] Is this for real?

00:01:55.763 --> 00:01:57.423
- Yes, now clean out your des.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:02.250
I removed the 'K' so you'd
understand how absurd ya sound.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.083
- [Jake] Oh boy.

00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:05.050
- Look him in the eye and
tell him what you did.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.220
- I didn't do it, Kevin.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.060
- Don't you say his name.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.350
No, Terry, I'm not mad at you,

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.630
I know you didn't mean to do it.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.760
You just got hungry

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.960
and that's the most
natural thing in the world.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.050
- I didn't take your pie.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.600
- You're lying!

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.910
- I don't always
understand Peralta's texts.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:22.720
He says their still waiting on
the lab and "it's allz good."

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.380
Alls with a "z".

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.720
Then a box with a question mark inside,

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.040
another box with a question mark,

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.430
another box with a question mark,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.930
another box with a question mark,

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.300
another box with a question mark

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.830
and yet, another box with a question mark,

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.400
then, a box with a question mark.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.400
What does that mean?

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.603
- It means you don't have
emoji's on your phone.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.740
- Good news is our evaluation will be done

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.580
by Deputy Chief Brant.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.180
We have a good rapport,
he was once my Captain.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.973
- So, he's kinda like our Grand-captain.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.393
- That is amazingly funny.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.593
Oh, I've caused a problem.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.490
I think I am...

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.640
getting a text message.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.623
Bloop.

00:03:05.623 --> 00:03:06.743
There it is.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.190
(sobbing)

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.893
- Captain, get in here.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.536
- There, there.

00:03:15.536 --> 00:03:17.225
There, there.

00:03:17.225 --> 00:03:18.210
There.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.043
- I'm coming in.

00:03:19.922 --> 00:03:21.980
(sobbing loudly)
- Oh Boyle.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.563
- Thank you for this honor, Deputy Chief.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.443
- Oh, okay.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:30.753
You're welcome.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.200
- Lunch time is over.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.315
Boom! Did it!

00:03:34.315 --> 00:03:35.960
(laughs) Had it both ways.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.324
No regrets.

00:03:37.324 --> 00:03:38.893
Go Razzmatazz.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.040
Go Razzmatazz.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.130
Go Razzmatazz.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.450
- [TV Announcer] It's Bugle
Boy, winning by a head.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.879
- I lost everything.

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:49.040
(gentle recorder music)
Now, the recorder

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.810
is generally thought of
as a training instrument

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.480
for children but, listen to her.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.930
In the hands of an expert
like Larum Layethgroom,

00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.820
the passion is...

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:01.723
breathtaking.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.310
- Wait, before you say anything

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.250
I wanna guess what happened
based on your face.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.180
Someone died?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.210
No, you won a prize!

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:12.370
I'm not getting better at this.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.790
- The next chart shows the drop

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.159
in the crime rate over the last month.

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:17.326
(beeping)

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:22.350
I just erased everything.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.580
Thank you.
- You're welcome.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:27.670
Team pop and lock, here we go.
(mimicking robotic noise)

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:28.800
Come on, still?

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.023
We saved your life.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.670
- Oh my god.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.630
Oh my god...

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.476
it's happening.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:39.140
Yes, we did it!
(cheering)

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.283
- Kitchen buds.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.820
- You all right, Captain?

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.290
Tough weekend?

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.660
- I went to Barbados with my husband.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.080
We wove hats out of palm fronds

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.530
and swam with the sting rays.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.690
I've never been happier.

00:04:56.468 --> 00:04:59.460
- Guy's impossible to
read, don't even try.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.550
- That is, without question,

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.091
the funniest story I've ever heard.

00:05:03.091 --> 00:05:04.120
- Mm, yeah.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.770
- Great, I hope there's a
lot of drug activity there.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.680
Of course, ideally, there will
be nobody taking drugs there

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:12.910
or anywhere else in this district,

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.240
but, if drugs must be
found, let it be there.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.890
Please God, let it be there.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.640
Resume the drill Timmy, and
do not do or say anything

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.680
that a seven year old
boy would not do or say.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.790
Feel free to consult the
script I've prepared.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.423
- Okay, but, it's a little stilted.

00:05:29.547 --> 00:05:31.517
"I am feeling trepidation at the prospect

00:05:31.517 --> 00:05:33.590
"of a parentless existence."

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:34.920
No kid talks like that.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.000
- Those lines were lifted,
verbatim, from my boyhood diary.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:38.963
Resume the drill!

00:05:40.536 --> 00:05:41.720
(singing) Duh, duh, duh.

00:05:45.368 --> 00:05:46.410
- What are you doing?

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.160
- Nothing, just enjoying a taste

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.310
of my favorite beverage, the soda pop.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.340
- Really?

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.173
I've never seen you
enjoy a soda pop before.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.133
Have some now.

00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:09.110
(fake satisfied sighing)

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:10.390
- It's delicious.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.260
Sergeant, I would like you
to meet Richard and Dan.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.760
They are puppies.

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.020
- Very cute, sir.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:19.927
- Maybe your twins would like
some little furry friends?

00:06:19.927 --> 00:06:21.160
- I'm sorry, sir.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.620
But, that's impossible.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.860
With the twins learning how to walk,

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.230
chaos reigns at the Jefford's household.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:29.180
I can't let those innocent
pups into that madhouse!

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.710
Terry won't do ya like that!

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:31.940
- I understand.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.410
Just know, you have disappointed...

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.933
all three of us.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:39.853
- That's cold, sir.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:43.553
- Go.

00:06:43.553 --> 00:06:44.500
(clearing throat)

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.350
- Marcus, I think we should break up.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.300
- That makes me feel sad.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.330
I am sad.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:53.070
- Your sadness is noted.
- I feel acknowledged.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.680
Thank you for breaking up with me.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.963
It will take me eight
minutes to collect my things.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.233
I think that went very well.

00:06:59.233 --> 00:07:00.620
- Hmm.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.140
- Great idea, take a breather.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:04.230
That was way too personal.

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.130
No one needs to know you have sisters.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.743
New topic, the moons of Jupiter.

00:07:10.159 --> 00:07:11.623
- I think I might be pregnant.

00:07:13.184 --> 00:07:16.130
- Oh.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.971
Oh!

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:19.804
Oh...

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.210
no.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.803
I am good at emotion.

00:07:28.401 --> 00:07:30.734
(smooching)

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.140
What the...

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.190
- Fine, I'll say I'm sorry.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.450
- No, be sincere, like this.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.430
I'm sorry.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:43.490
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.750
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.810
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:49.180
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.540
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.373
- I'm sorry.

00:07:51.373 --> 00:07:52.520
- Good, that's the one.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.320
- I've been craving Sudanese all day.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.418
I'll print out some menus.

00:07:57.418 --> 00:07:58.593
(thudding)
- Ouch.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:00.970
You ran over my foot.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.283
I am in incredible pain.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.650
- All right!
(group cheering)

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:08.710
- Does anyone have a few
words they would like to say?

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:09.547
- No one say anything,

00:08:09.547 --> 00:08:11.768
I want him to say stuff.

00:08:11.768 --> 00:08:13.540
Speech for Jake.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.451
Speech for Jake, go!
- Very well.

00:08:15.451 --> 00:08:18.670
Your six month absence was noted.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:21.680
Drinks are on me, there's a
two drink maximum per person.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.264
- Here he goes.
- It is nontransferable.

00:08:23.264 --> 00:08:25.260
You're guests will pay their own tab.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:26.560
- Oh, yeah.
- Valet parking

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.160
is not included.
- Solid protocol.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.770
- Tomorrows briefing will be
15 minutes earlier than usual.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:33.710
- He's so bad ass.
- And I'm very proud

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:34.543
of you Peralta.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:36.767
We missed you.

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:38.250
- Aw, you ruined it.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.062
- No, no, I said millimeter.

00:08:40.062 --> 00:08:43.274
(loud laughing)

00:08:43.274 --> 00:08:45.630
- Okay, I'm gonna choke from laughter.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.811
You're too funny!

00:08:47.811 --> 00:08:48.693
- New plan.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:51.370
I'm gonna charm her.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:54.770
- Oh, no.

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:56.560
- I'm sorry, I had to take that.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.860
- You gotta do what you gotta do.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:08:59.910
Captain Raymond Holt.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.646
What's up?

00:09:02.646 --> 00:09:05.229
(sultry music)

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.230
- Well, how do you even
know he's in a bad mood?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.167
I mean, its impossible to read that guy.

00:09:10.167 --> 00:09:13.330
- This is the most
incompetent worthless report

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.220
I have ever read in my life!

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.540
Get your act together or so help me God,

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.423
you won't live to see retirement!

00:09:20.369 --> 00:09:22.690
(door slams)
Good, he's gone.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.813
Now, lets get serious and focus up.

00:09:24.813 --> 00:09:28.050
(thumping and springing)

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.981
Just trying to get to the printer.

00:09:29.981 --> 00:09:32.970
- (singing) Cream in my
coffee and rock and roll.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:34.580
- Peralta.
- Ah, Captain Holt!

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.330
You look very...

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.163
sad.

00:09:37.163 --> 00:09:37.996
I can never tell.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.100
- It must be very difficult.

00:09:44.739 --> 00:09:46.530
- Wait, are you crying?

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:47.363
- Yes.

00:09:50.117 --> 00:09:52.430
Thank you for acknowledging my feelings.

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.780
- Thank you for acknowledging mine.

00:09:56.553 --> 00:09:58.712
- We're both great at this.

00:09:58.712 --> 00:10:01.160
(crying and sniffling)

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.550
- You look chipper, Captain.

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:03.740
You have a fun weekend?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.640
- There was a small fire in my home.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.293
I lost many photo albums
of treasured memories.

00:10:09.429 --> 00:10:10.940
I'm devastated.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.320
- Any smile that lasts longer
than a second and a half

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.620
is a conman's ruse.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:17.453
- Fake.
- That's fake.

00:10:17.453 --> 00:10:18.630
- That's a fake one.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.207
- I said it.

00:10:20.207 --> 00:10:21.375
And I meant it!

00:10:21.375 --> 00:10:22.870
(cheering)

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:23.995
- Great work team!

00:10:23.995 --> 00:10:26.578
(upbeat music)

